---
import ContentPage from "../components/ContentPage.astro";
---

<ContentPage
	title="How It Works | Resize Photo for PAN Card"
	description="Learn how to resize PAN card photos and signatures using NSDL/Protean or UTIITSL presets, review the JPEG, then verify current portal requirements."
	canonicalUrl="https://nsdlphotoresize.com/how-it-works/"
	eyebrow="Step-by-step guide"
	heading="How to resize a photo and signature for PAN card"
	intro="Use this PAN card document resizer online to crop your image, choose dimensions, and prepare a JPEG in a few steps. Your image stays in your browser throughout editing."
>
	<ol class="space-y-8">
		<li class="space-y-3">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">1. Choose an image</h2>
			<p>
				Open the <a class="text-link" href="/#photo-tool">photo resizer</a>&nbsp;
				and select a JPG, PNG, or WebP file from your device. Choose
				Photograph or Signature, then select NSDL/Protean or UTIITSL
				to load the relevant dimensions, resolution, file-size limit,
				and capture guidance.
			</p>
		</li>
		<li class="space-y-3">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">2. Set dimensions and crop</h2>
			<p>
				Choose the matching portal preset or adjust the width, height,
				and resolution to the current application instructions. The
				NSDL/Protean reference dimensions are 2.5 × 3.5 cm for a photo
				and 4.5 × 2 cm for a signature, both at 200 DPI. UTIITSL uses
				213 × 213 px at 300 DPI for a photo and 400 × 200 px at 600
				DPI for a signature. Drag the crop box to position the image
				and review the pixel preview.
			</p>
		</li>
		<li class="space-y-3">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">3. Review and download</h2>
			<p>
				Check the output dimensions and file size, then download the
				JPEG. The selected preset sets the file-size limit: NSDL/
				Protean is 50 KB for both images; UTIITSL is 30 KB for a photo
				and 60 KB for a signature. If the image cannot meet its limit
				at minimum quality, try a simpler or clearer source image.
			</p>
		</li>
		<li class="space-y-3">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">4. Verify before uploading</h2>
			<p>
				Open the saved image and confirm the crop is right. Compare its
				format, dimensions, resolution, and size against the current
				instructions on the official Protean or UTIITSL portal. An NSDL
				photo resize or UTI photo resize workflow does not replace the
				portal’s own requirements.
			</p>
		</li>
	</ol>
	<p>
		All image editing takes place in your browser. The tool does not upload
		or overwrite your original image, and preparing a file does not
		guarantee acceptance of an application.
	</p>
</ContentPage>
